course: dictionary
lesson: 12456
title: Defensive: protecting against attack
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word defensive is linked to defend, which means to protect something from harm. When you meet it, read the words around it for clues. «The knight raised a defensive shield to block the arrows.» Shields block arrows, so defensive means used to protect against attack.
explain: Defensive can also describe a person. «When Sam was told he had spelled a word wrong, he got defensive and said, "It's not my fault!"» Sam is protecting himself from feeling blamed, so defensive means reacting as if you are being criticised or attacked.
explain: In sport, defensive means about stopping the other team from scoring. «The defensive players kept the ball away from our goal.» Check your meaning by swapping it in: "protecting" fits the sentence, so your meaning works.
fact: Defensive means used or made to protect against attack, like «a defensive wall».
fact: A defensive person reacts as if they are being criticised or attacked, and tries to protect themselves.
fact: In sport, «defensive» means about stopping the other team from scoring.
fact: Useful phrases include «defensive player», «defensive wall», «on the defensive» and «get defensive».
fact: In nature, animals can have defensive features, like spines and shells.
exercise: «The castle had thick defensive walls and a deep moat.» What does defensive mean here? | Very tall and pointed | Used for cooking big feasts | *Used to protect against attack | Made of wood and painted
exercise: «Mia got defensive when her friend pointed out her mistake.» What does defensive mean in this sentence? | *Reacting as if she was under attack | Running very fast to catch up | Speaking in a loud, cheerful voice | Feeling very happy about the mistake
exercise: «The defensive players stopped the other team from scoring.» What was the job of the defensive players? | Watching the clock | Scoring as many goals as possible | *Stopping the other team from scoring | Cheering for the crowd
test: «After the teacher asked about the spilt paint, Jo was on the defensive.» What does on the defensive mean? | Happy that the mess was found | Feeling sleepy after a long day | *Ready to protect herself, expecting to be criticised | Holding a paintbrush in her hand
test: Which of these is a defensive feature in nature? | *Sharp spines that protect against attack | Bright colours to attract a mate | A long tail for swimming fast | Big ears for hearing better
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to defensive, when it means protecting against attack? | Sleepy | Loud | Playful | *Protective
